WEBVTT

00:01.330 --> 00:05.000
I'm guessing you had to go through hell last night.

00:05.750 --> 00:09.000
I was scared, but I made a promise.

00:11.750 --> 00:12.920
I love you, you know.

00:18.420 --> 00:19.330
Me, too.

00:20.420 --> 00:22.670
I love you, too.

00:25.460 --> 00:29.540
So I promise, no matter what happens,
or what we get tangled up in,

00:30.750 --> 00:33.000
I will always come to save you.

00:34.330 --> 00:35.130
Good.

00:36.250 --> 00:39.040
Kei-kun, I've got you now.

00:41.830 --> 00:43.750
Yayoi-chan, I made my decision.

00:44.250 --> 00:46.080
I'll help you catch spirits.

00:47.250 --> 00:48.080
You sure?

00:48.460 --> 00:49.040
I'm sure.

00:49.540 --> 00:53.080
All this time, I was so afraid
of getting other people tangled up in this,

00:53.080 --> 00:55.380
so I thought it was better to be alone.

00:57.420 --> 00:58.080
But now,

00:58.790 --> 01:01.380
I can push through that fear
because I want to protect the ones I love!

01:06.000 --> 01:06.920
Good.

01:08.830 --> 01:11.960
Welcome to the dark side.

01:12.710 --> 01:15.670
Thanks. Just watch my back, Yayoi-chan.

01:19.540 --> 01:21.330
Get home safe.

01:21.830 --> 01:22.670
Thanks.

01:23.290 --> 01:29.330
Right, I had a question.
Do you see groups of spirits like that often?

01:30.040 --> 01:30.920
Why're you asking?

01:31.210 --> 01:36.500
Just wanted to know so I can emotionally prepare myself.

01:36.880 --> 01:38.250
You're already scared.

01:39.580 --> 01:41.540
I mean, they're pretty rare.

01:42.420 --> 01:48.420
Spirits usually eat other spirits to stay
in this world longer, like we saw at Complex T.

01:49.290 --> 01:52.920
So grouping together usually means
they'll eat each other or steal food from one another.

01:54.460 --> 01:56.960
But that's not always the case.

01:58.080 --> 02:02.750
Some spirits don't know they're dead,
some are tied to certain locations,

02:03.460 --> 02:09.170
and some group together because they're scared
of a bigger threat in the area.

02:11.130 --> 02:15.210
Wait, so there could've been
an even nastier spirit by the campsite?

02:15.420 --> 02:17.380
I didn't see anything there.

02:18.210 --> 02:22.670
But I know of a spirit that nasty that wanders around.

02:23.000 --> 02:24.290
You do?

02:25.210 --> 02:27.000
The one who took Mommy.

02:28.540 --> 02:33.080
Based on its power and size, I've given it a name...

02:34.210 --> 02:36.670
a name taken from the story of the Hyakki Yagyo,

02:37.130 --> 02:39.920
where the parade of thousands of supernatural baddies
are burned to death by the sun.

02:40.580 --> 02:42.000
I call it...

02:43.170 --> 02:45.130
...the Spectre of Death.

02:51.710 --> 02:53.080
Yayoi-chan...

02:54.420 --> 03:02.420
While we walk the world of the living,
the dead drift through the spirit world.

03:03.290 --> 03:09.960
These two worlds sometimes intersect,
allowing evil spirits to do harm to the living.

03:10.880 --> 03:18.420
This young girl is gathering dark power
to slay the spirit who took her loved one.

03:16.080 --> 03:20.670
<b>FATAL CRASHES</b>

03:16.080 --> 03:20.670
<b>IN THIS AREA</b>

03:19.130 --> 03:24.130
The grudges of the dead,
used to pursue a grudge far greater...

04:56.580 --> 05:00.830
The pink of falling cherry blossoms was soon replaced
by the bright green of spring leaves,

05:01.670 --> 05:04.710
and I made my fateful decision
to dive back into the supernatural.

05:05.960 --> 05:09.880
Yayoi-chan is gathering spirits
to find the horror that took her mom.

05:10.880 --> 05:15.630
And I'm helping so I can get rid
of the curse that plagues Eiko and I.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.960
You know this works, Keitaro?

05:19.960 --> 05:20.710
Yeah.

05:21.540 --> 05:24.630
Using your spirit magnetism as a conduit,

05:25.080 --> 05:29.710
we pray for the gods to lead us in the right direction,

05:31.330 --> 05:33.000
and that will determine where to go.

05:33.830 --> 05:36.630
Before we go, we have studying to do, Yayoi-chan.

05:36.830 --> 05:38.500
Keitaro, you're no fun.

05:38.710 --> 05:39.830
It's less about the studying.

05:40.330 --> 05:43.580
The later we go, the more likely
we'll see something, right?

05:45.630 --> 05:48.080
You're scary cool tonight, Keitaro.

05:48.500 --> 05:50.710
As long as I can push through my fear...

05:51.130 --> 05:56.080
there's nothing holding me back
from going to all these haunted places!

06:00.460 --> 06:04.330
That's everything for today. Good job.

06:04.750 --> 06:05.880
Piece of cake.

06:07.630 --> 06:09.710
Okay, let's head out.

06:16.630 --> 06:17.630
Get in.

06:18.330 --> 06:20.420
Looks like SOMEONE is super excited to go!

06:20.790 --> 06:22.630
Where to, little lady?

06:22.880 --> 06:23.580
Here.

06:23.710 --> 06:25.960
Oh? Is it finally time?!

06:25.960 --> 06:26.790
Uh-huh.

06:27.460 --> 06:29.170
Okay. Ready?

06:29.630 --> 06:31.130
Let's gooo...

06:31.130 --> 06:32.040
...ooost!

06:33.330 --> 06:35.210
Haven't heard that in a while.

06:39.630 --> 06:45.170
I didn't really want Eiko coming with us
to haunted places, but...

06:45.460 --> 06:50.960
Stay with me. Don't go off on your own.
Stay close, so we can work together.

06:51.170 --> 06:54.080
I made a promise, and I intend to keep it.

06:54.750 --> 07:00.210
Besides, if I mess stuff up with Eiko now,
my life is totally forfeit!

07:03.380 --> 07:06.130
Oh, God. I can't ring her doorbell.

07:06.630 --> 07:11.880
After our conversation at the river,
we're basically dating now, right? Or am I wrong?

07:12.830 --> 07:15.630
I still can't believe I said all that embarrassing stuff!

07:15.960 --> 07:18.210
"I'll always come save you." Kill me!

07:18.210 --> 07:20.210
How can I even face her?!

07:20.210 --> 07:21.130
Please!

07:21.130 --> 07:23.040
Yayoi-chan, please be Yayoi-chan!

07:23.380 --> 07:25.920
Kei-kun, there you are!

07:29.790 --> 07:34.580
I am the gatekeeper of the Hozuki Manse!
What is the password, good sir?

07:34.830 --> 07:37.330
Hint: It's what you and I are to one another!

07:37.330 --> 07:38.880
SHE GOT STRAIGHT TO THE POINT!

07:39.170 --> 07:43.630
Just so you know, "bestie," "savior,"
and "childhood friend" are all off the table!

07:43.790 --> 07:45.380
She's got me cornered!

07:45.830 --> 07:48.790
Sh-should I say we're dating, then?!

07:51.710 --> 07:52.460
Flashback.

07:52.460 --> 07:55.130
I love you, too.

07:55.330 --> 07:57.630
So I promise, no matter what happens...

07:55.330 --> 07:58.210
SHE RECORDED IT?!

07:58.210 --> 07:59.130
C'mon!

07:59.250 --> 08:02.670
I-I do believe w-we are what some may call "dating"...

08:02.670 --> 08:03.670
Three words!

08:05.250 --> 08:07.040
Boyfriend... and girlfriend.

08:08.880 --> 08:11.460
Yep! You may pass!

08:11.710 --> 08:15.710
Also, I've got that clip set as my wake-up alarm.

08:15.710 --> 08:16.630
Please don't!

08:17.290 --> 08:19.290
I'm gonna cringe myself to death!

08:19.540 --> 08:21.210
I gotta keep her happy!

08:21.920 --> 08:26.460
Stay calm. If something bad happens,
I'll just make sure she's kept safe.

08:26.830 --> 08:29.250
I have the power to sense
that bad stuff before it happens!

08:30.080 --> 08:32.750
Keitaro, you don't have to stress out so much.

08:34.380 --> 08:35.460
I'm here, too.

08:36.830 --> 08:38.040
Yayoi-chan...

08:39.250 --> 08:44.420
I want to learn how to protect people, too, and soon,
so I can be just as much help as she is...

08:45.290 --> 08:46.580
We're almost here!

08:47.000 --> 08:50.170
Eiko, you already know the place?

08:50.170 --> 08:53.920
Uh-huh. It's one of the more famous haunted spots.

08:55.960 --> 09:01.920
There've been tons of TV shows
and articles about it over the last fifty years,

09:02.130 --> 09:05.210
all calling it the "spookiest place in the city."

09:06.290 --> 09:08.750
This is it: S Tunnel.

09:11.250 --> 09:14.790
There's a bunch of stories about it,
all first-person accounts, apparently.

09:16.000 --> 09:22.000
A long-haired woman in a white dress,
covered in blood, wanders the length of the tunnel.

09:22.670 --> 09:26.460
A woman and her child cross in front
of your car as it drives through.

09:27.790 --> 09:33.040
Your back mirror fills with the image of someone
crawling towards you, hand raised.

09:33.210 --> 09:35.170
But when you turn to look, nothing is there!

09:36.420 --> 09:42.960
An upside-down woman stares at the driver,
then falls on the hood of the car and starts chasing you!

09:43.880 --> 09:48.000
Hands reach out from the walls
to grab anyone walking past!

09:48.790 --> 09:51.580
Most of these are talking about a female spirit.

09:54.830 --> 09:56.080
I'm hype.

09:56.080 --> 09:57.420
Oh, totally!

09:57.630 --> 09:59.170
Let's go!

09:59.170 --> 10:01.130
Wait, you're gonna film it?

10:01.380 --> 10:03.080
Yeah, why not?

10:03.460 --> 10:06.040
Don't blame me if you capture something creepy!

10:06.380 --> 10:07.290
I can't wait.

10:07.290 --> 10:08.170
Same!

10:10.460 --> 10:13.580
Let's traverse it on foot to see if those stories are true.

10:16.880 --> 10:21.080
The tunnel gets a lot of traffic,
so the lights make it pretty bright in here.

10:21.290 --> 10:22.130
Yeah.

10:25.290 --> 10:28.290
<b>ROAD WORK</b>

10:25.290 --> 10:28.290
<b>AHEAD</b>

10:37.460 --> 10:38.830
Wh-what happened?

10:39.080 --> 10:41.040
Sorry, the water scared me.

10:41.500 --> 10:43.670
Oh, okay. Let's keep going.

10:43.920 --> 10:44.790
Yeah.

10:49.580 --> 10:53.710
Here I thought she liked scary stuff.
Her reactions tonight are adorable.

10:54.330 --> 10:57.130
Don't worry, Eiko. Yayoi-chan and I are here.

11:00.670 --> 11:04.290
Oh, sorry, my camera started acting up...

11:04.790 --> 11:09.080
C'mon, how am I out of battery? Not now!

11:09.080 --> 11:12.250
Hold on. If she's there...

11:13.080 --> 11:15.420
...then whose hand am I holding?

11:26.170 --> 11:28.000
Kei-kun, are you okay?!

11:30.000 --> 11:30.880
It's gone.

11:31.710 --> 11:34.540
But I still feel its presence.

11:35.330 --> 11:37.500
Let's leave and come back in the car.

11:37.500 --> 11:38.330
Huh?!
Okay!<b></b>

11:39.080 --> 11:41.670
Can we go home yet?

12:00.750 --> 12:02.540
Let's do this again!

12:03.250 --> 12:06.330
This time, to see what happens when we drive through!

12:07.790 --> 12:10.960
Wait, we're not going all the way through?
Why are we stopping?!

12:10.960 --> 12:13.580
Because we want the ghost to come after us. Duh.

12:13.580 --> 12:15.670
Oh. Right.

12:15.670 --> 12:18.380
I forgot we were here to capture it.

12:18.790 --> 12:23.830
The stereotype is for the ghost
to end up in the car with you.

12:23.960 --> 12:29.460
But most stories say ghosts can't enter your home
if you don't open the door for them.

12:29.460 --> 12:31.250
Eek, scary!

12:34.750 --> 12:37.540
I don't see the woman with a child crossing before us.

12:37.790 --> 12:40.750
Could've just been the wind?

12:40.750 --> 12:41.790
Maybe.

12:42.210 --> 12:44.290
I definitely sense something, though.

12:50.040 --> 12:51.080
Someone's hurt back there!

12:54.130 --> 12:55.040
Did you see something?

12:55.540 --> 12:59.290
Yeah, I saw someone hurt
on the road behind us in our mirror,

13:00.170 --> 13:01.290
but now they're gone.

13:03.880 --> 13:09.960
That kinda sounds like that story
about the woman crawling towards the car.

13:11.670 --> 13:14.960
Think logically! When we drove in, no one was there!

13:15.290 --> 13:16.670
Wanna go back and look again?

13:16.670 --> 13:18.460
Uh, no, not really!

13:18.460 --> 13:19.500
Back we go, then.

13:20.040 --> 13:22.080
Okie-dokie! About-face!

13:43.130 --> 13:44.080
H-holy shit...

13:43.790 --> 13:45.380
Why'd you do that?!

13:45.540 --> 13:48.630
I had to test to see what type she was.

13:50.170 --> 13:54.500
When a spirit's hit by a car,
there are three things that could happen.

13:55.250 --> 13:57.250
One, it passes through.

13:57.250 --> 13:57.630
<b>SHOOP</b>

13:58.580 --> 14:01.380
Two, it passes through and stays in the car.

14:00.750 --> 14:01.250
<b>HI!</b>

14:02.330 --> 14:04.250
Three, it gets hit.

14:04.000 --> 14:04.500
<b>OWIE!</b>

14:05.830 --> 14:09.080
This one got hit, which gives us info.

14:09.830 --> 14:16.080
It wants to mess with us,
but unless we let it in, it can't get into the car.

14:16.920 --> 14:17.750
So...

14:18.630 --> 14:19.710
You're letting it in?!

14:20.040 --> 14:21.290
It's already in.

14:22.130 --> 14:25.130
Keitaro, on your left! Get it with this doll!

14:25.130 --> 14:26.460
Wait, what?!

14:27.920 --> 14:31.920
Hurry! Right! Up top! Now sideways! Lower right!

14:33.170 --> 14:36.000
We caught it...

14:36.710 --> 14:38.580
Don't stop choking its neck with that rice straw rope.

14:39.000 --> 14:40.920
It's just as strong as salt.

14:41.170 --> 14:42.290
Got it.

14:42.290 --> 14:44.540
Wait, you caught it?

14:45.000 --> 14:46.330
Yep. Time to go home.

14:47.130 --> 14:49.170
She's bringing it home? To our house?!

14:50.830 --> 14:53.040
Can't believe everything went well again.

14:53.540 --> 14:56.630
Though I can't shake this bad feeling...

15:04.500 --> 15:07.790
A-am I just imagining things? I must be.

15:16.500 --> 15:18.630
Okay, have a good night!

15:18.790 --> 15:21.170
I will, thanks. Good night!

15:22.670 --> 15:23.710
Hey, Mom.

15:25.420 --> 15:26.790
There you are!

15:27.170 --> 15:27.920
Yep.

15:39.330 --> 15:42.080
Man, another day of being scared out of my mind...

15:42.670 --> 15:44.960
And I still feel like something's not right.

15:52.170 --> 15:56.040
I was so worried about going, but it all turned out fine.

15:56.250 --> 15:58.670
If this keeps up, I'll be more comfortable in no time.

16:15.830 --> 16:16.750
Yayoi-chan?

16:17.040 --> 16:18.000
We've been duped.

16:18.500 --> 16:19.250
Huh?

16:19.960 --> 16:22.420
We caught a random wandering spirit.

16:22.830 --> 16:23.630
Really?!

16:24.170 --> 16:26.580
It's possible she used an illusion.

16:27.580 --> 16:28.750
Like the one at the temple.

16:29.710 --> 16:32.080
This spirit made us think we'd got her...

16:33.080 --> 16:36.080
Which means we'd let our guard down around her.

16:36.750 --> 16:38.500
And she's doing that for a reason.

16:38.500 --> 16:40.130
What reason?

16:40.750 --> 16:42.540
This one's extremely cunning.

16:43.710 --> 16:45.580
We need to go back to Keitaro's.

16:50.170 --> 16:54.000
What the hell is wrong with you?! It's half past midnight!

16:54.000 --> 16:56.080
Wait, Eiko-chan?

16:56.880 --> 17:02.000
Long time no see, Mrs. Gentoga!
Sorry to bother you so late.

17:02.420 --> 17:04.210
Sure. What is it?

17:04.750 --> 17:05.880
Hello, ma'am.

17:06.750 --> 17:09.460
My name is Yayoi, I'm Eiko's cousin.

17:09.460 --> 17:13.580
Keitaro-sensei is my tutor,
and he's already taught me a lot.

17:14.330 --> 17:19.040
He took the wrong phone with him when he left today, 
and I was worried he needed his tonight.

17:19.790 --> 17:24.330
Would it be alright if I came inside to give him his phone?

17:24.540 --> 17:28.670
Goodness, is that right?
Thank you for coming over so late.

17:28.880 --> 17:30.790
Please, come in.

17:31.170 --> 17:32.290
Thank you, ma'am.

17:33.500 --> 17:34.750
Thank you.

17:36.040 --> 17:40.790
What a sweet girl. I'm glad you've got
such a nice student, Keitaro!

17:43.330 --> 17:44.330
Piece of cake.

17:44.630 --> 17:46.880
You didn't even bat an eye...

17:47.080 --> 17:50.080
<b>Keitaro</b>

17:53.710 --> 17:54.500
Wait.

18:26.420 --> 18:29.000
I knew it. That one's an illusion.

18:30.080 --> 18:32.670
I'm glad we took the time to double-check.

18:34.960 --> 18:36.830
It's right next to the door.

18:38.380 --> 18:39.380
I can touch it.

19:08.000 --> 19:09.250
Let go of Keitaro.

19:24.380 --> 19:25.880
I didn't say I'd let you go.

19:27.750 --> 19:31.290
You tried to kill someone. Now you pay the price.

19:35.830 --> 19:38.880
This time, I caught you.

19:47.710 --> 19:49.210
What's up, Keitaro?

19:49.540 --> 19:52.080
Nothing, just had a really bad dream last night.

19:52.540 --> 19:54.540
It's been bothering me all day.

19:54.830 --> 19:56.080
What was it about?

19:56.420 --> 20:01.750
It's definitely because we went to the tunnel.
It was about a female ghost dragging me away.

20:03.670 --> 20:05.170
That actually happened.

20:05.170 --> 20:05.790
Wait.

20:06.710 --> 20:09.630
REALLY?!

20:09.880 --> 20:12.420
Yep. Here she is.

20:15.080 --> 20:16.710
I can't believe it.

20:17.580 --> 20:21.750
Here I was supposed to be helping.
Instead, I just keep making more work for you.

20:22.210 --> 20:23.880
No, you're not.

20:25.130 --> 20:30.420
Ever since I met you last month,
I've caught way more spirits than ever before.

20:31.290 --> 20:35.210
We each have different jobs on our team.

20:35.830 --> 20:38.170
As long as we do those jobs well, we're good.

20:39.380 --> 20:40.710
You've been really helpful...

20:42.420 --> 20:43.670
Yayoi-chan...!

20:45.080 --> 20:46.250
...as a decoy.

20:46.330 --> 20:46.960
Wha-?

20:47.500 --> 20:50.170
You're the best decoy. My scaredy-cat, chicken decoy.
Come on, Yayoi-chan! I'm better than that!<b></b>

20:50.170 --> 20:51.500
Stop calling me chicken!

20:54.750 --> 20:55.880
Thanks for having me.

20:56.500 --> 20:57.750
Wait, Keitaro.

20:58.170 --> 20:59.880
Lemme see your backpack.

21:06.500 --> 21:09.130
Sheesh. I can't take my eyes off you for a second.

21:09.880 --> 21:12.330
Next time you try this, you're getting punished.

21:12.830 --> 21:16.040
Okay, now you can go.

21:24.420 --> 21:25.170
I gotta get home.

21:30.880 --> 21:32.880
Hello, this is Gentoga.

21:33.830 --> 21:35.830
Uh-huh. Yes, thank you, sir.

21:36.710 --> 21:37.670
Right.

21:39.080 --> 21:42.170
Wait, a new student? For me?!

23:22.250 --> 23:27.080
Keitaro gets a new tutoring student.

23:28.040 --> 23:33.210
She, too, has her own concerns
about the supernatural, and her own loneliness.

23:34.460 --> 23:39.920
What do the stars in her eyes foretell?
